<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CI-ONLY Maven settings for the GitHub Packages publish chain. Passed explicitly with
  `-s .github/maven-ci-settings.xml` by .github/workflows/release.yml and by NOTHING else.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS INSTEAD OF A <repositories> BLOCK IN pom.xml
  ================================================================
  maven.pkg.github.com requires authentication even to READ. Measured 2026-09-17 from a
  developer box, against a coordinate that may or may not exist — the point is the status
  code, which is identical either way:

      $ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' \
          https://maven.pkg.github.com/hugmesh/hugmesh-parent/net/hugmesh/hugmesh-parent/2.8.0/hugmesh-parent-2.8.0.pom
      401
      $ curl ... -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gh auth token)" ...   # classic token, no read:packages
      401

  So declaring that URL in pom.xml would make EVERY unauthenticated build fail — a
  developer's `./mvnw verify`, and hugmesh-generator/tests/stack/m2-bootstrap.sh, which is
  how the compose lane builds these libraries today (from pinned SHAs, deliberately NOT
  from a registry). Decision 27 keeps that source-build mechanism unchanged. The publish
  path is prepared, not switched on. A settings file passed with `-s` is the only shape
  that adds a repository for CI without adding one for everybody.

  ReleaseMetadataGuardTest fails the build if maven.pkg.github.com ever appears in pom.xml
  or in the repo-root settings.xml (the GitLab one). That guard is the thing standing
  between this design and someone "simplifying" it back into the pom.

  BOTH <repositories> AND <pluginRepositories>, deliberately
  =========================================================
  net.hugmesh:hugmesh-build-config is not a project dependency. hugmesh-parent adds it to
  the maven-pmd-plugin / maven-checkstyle-plugin / spotbugs-maven-plugin <dependencies>
  blocks so each analyser reads the curated ruleset off its own plugin classloader. Maven
  resolves a PLUGIN's dependencies from the plugin repositories, not the project
  repositories — declaring the URL only under <repositories> resolves the parent POM and
  then dies at `verify` on the ruleset jar instead.

  WHY EACH REPOSITORY ID GETS ITS OWN <server>
  ============================================
  GitHub Packages is per-repository: https://maven.pkg.github.com/<owner>/<repo> serves the
  packages published from THAT repo only. There is no org-wide Maven endpoint, so the three
  upstream links of the chain are three URLs, and a <server> id must match each repository
  id for Maven to attach credentials. They all carry the same credential.

  AND WHY `github` IS IN HERE TOO
  ===============================
  `-s` REPLACES the user settings file, so the <server id="github"> that
  actions/setup-java writes into ~/.m2/settings.xml is NOT visible to a build run with this
  file. The deploy step's -DaltDeploymentRepository=github::default::... would then upload
  with no credential at all. The `github` server below is what keeps deploy authenticated.

  NO SECRET IS COMMITTED HERE. GITHUB_ACTOR and GITHUB_TOKEN are injected by the workflow
  from ${{ github.actor }} and the automatic ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}.

  THE UPSTREAM SERVERS DO NOT USE THE SAME CREDENTIAL AS THE DEPLOY SERVER
  =======================================================================
  `github` (deploy, this repo's own registry) authenticates with the automatic
  ${env.GITHUB_TOKEN}. That is correct and needs nothing from an operator: a workflow may
  always write packages for the repository it runs in.

  The `github-hugmesh-*` servers READ packages published from OTHER repositories, and the
  automatic GITHUB_TOKEN is scoped to the repository whose workflow is running. GitHub does
  not grant it cross-repository package access by default: the package has to name this
  repository under "Manage Actions access" in its own package settings, or the build has to
  present a token that carries read:packages for the owner. Wiring these servers to
  ${env.GITHUB_TOKEN} would therefore work only if somebody remembered to click the grant,
  and would fail as `Could not resolve net.hugmesh:...`, the exact string this repo's docs
  teach a reader to interpret as "the upstream is not published yet". That misdiagnosis is
  the cost this split exists to avoid.

  So the read credential is its own env var. release.yml injects
      UPSTREAM_PACKAGES_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.PACKAGES_READ_TOKEN || secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
  which means: use the operator's read:packages PAT if one exists, otherwise fall back to
  the automatic token (correct once the per-package Actions-access grant is in place). The
  "Preflight, cross-repo package read" step in release.yml probes the upstream registries
  with this credential BEFORE maven runs, and reports an authorisation failure as an
  authorisation failure. RELEASING.md section 6.2 carries the operator's choice between the
  two routes. NEITHER IS VERIFIED. No CI job in this org has ever started (billing).
-->
<settings xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0"
          xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/settings-1.0.0.xsd">

  <servers>
    <!-- Deploy target for THIS repo (the -DaltDeploymentRepository id). -->
    <server>
      <id>github</id>
      <username>${env.GITHUB_ACTOR}</username>
      <password>${env.GITHUB_TOKEN}</password>
    </server>
    <!-- Read credentials for the three upstream links of the chain. -->
    <server>
      <id>github-hugmesh-build-config</id>
      <username>${env.UPSTREAM_PACKAGES_ACTOR}</username>
      <password>${env.UPSTREAM_PACKAGES_TOKEN}</password>
    </server>
    <server>
      <id>github-hugmesh-parent</id>
      <username>${env.UPSTREAM_PACKAGES_ACTOR}</username>
      <password>${env.UPSTREAM_PACKAGES_TOKEN}</password>
    </server>
    <server>
      <id>github-hugmesh-commons</id>
      <username>${env.UPSTREAM_PACKAGES_ACTOR}</username>
      <password>${env.UPSTREAM_PACKAGES_TOKEN}</password>
    </server>
  </servers>

  <profiles>
    <profile>
      <id>github-hugmesh-packages</id>

      <!-- Project dependencies + the parent POM. Parent resolution is the reason this has
           to be in settings.xml at all: a <repositories> block inside pom.xml cannot be
           used to resolve that same pom's own <parent>. -->
      <repositories>
        <repository>
          <id>github-hugmesh-build-config</id>
          <url>https://maven.pkg.github.com/hugmesh/hugmesh-build-config</url>
          <releases><enabled>true</enabled></releases>
          <snapshots><enabled>false</enabled></snapshots>
        </repository>
        <repository>
          <id>github-hugmesh-parent</id>
          <url>https://maven.pkg.github.com/hugmesh/hugmesh-parent</url>
          <releases><enabled>true</enabled></releases>
          <snapshots><enabled>false</enabled></snapshots>
        </repository>
        <repository>
          <id>github-hugmesh-commons</id>
          <url>https://maven.pkg.github.com/hugmesh/hugmesh-commons</url>
          <releases><enabled>true</enabled></releases>
          <snapshots><enabled>false</enabled></snapshots>
        </repository>
      </repositories>

      <!-- Plugin classpath artifacts — hugmesh-build-config's rulesets. See the header. -->
      <pluginRepositories>
        <pluginRepository>
          <id>github-hugmesh-build-config</id>
          <url>https://maven.pkg.github.com/hugmesh/hugmesh-build-config</url>
          <releases><enabled>true</enabled></releases>
          <snapshots><enabled>false</enabled></snapshots>
        </pluginRepository>
        <pluginRepository>
          <id>github-hugmesh-parent</id>
          <url>https://maven.pkg.github.com/hugmesh/hugmesh-parent</url>
          <releases><enabled>true</enabled></releases>
          <snapshots><enabled>false</enabled></snapshots>
        </pluginRepository>
        <pluginRepository>
          <id>github-hugmesh-commons</id>
          <url>https://maven.pkg.github.com/hugmesh/hugmesh-commons</url>
          <releases><enabled>true</enabled></releases>
          <snapshots><enabled>false</enabled></snapshots>
        </pluginRepository>
      </pluginRepositories>
    </profile>
  </profiles>

  <!-- Active unconditionally: this file only ever reaches a build that asked for it by
       path, so there is nothing to gate on. -->
  <activeProfiles>
    <activeProfile>github-hugmesh-packages</activeProfile>
  </activeProfiles>
</settings>
